        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(subagents): native announceTarget for subagent completion routing (#27445)",
        "body": "Fixes #27445\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nNative `sessions_spawn` subagent completions always announce to the channel via delivery-mirror. Orchestrator patterns need the completion to come back to the **parent session** as a normal trigger message instead — without any direct channel announce — so the parent can integrate results and decide what (if anything) the user sees. Current parent handoff behavior exists but is hard-coded by activity/thread state, not caller-selectable, and thread-bound `mode:\"session\"` spawns can register no completion announce at all.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdds native `announceTarget: \"channel\" | \"parent\"` to `sessions_spawn` (default `\"channel\"`, current behavior unchanged):\n\n- `\"parent\"` wakes the requester session once with `deliver:false` through the existing `subagent_announce` internal-event path — no direct channel announce, no fallback to channel on parent failure\n- Thread-bound `thread:true, mode:\"session\"` spawns with `announceTarget:\"parent\"` keep direct child-thread delivery for the active run but now register completion (addresses the edge raised in the issue comments)\n- Config precedence: per-spawn arg > `agents.list[].subagents.announceTarget` > `agents.defaults.subagents.announceTarget` > `\"channel\"`\n- `announceTarget` persists in the subagent registry (JSON + SQLite) so pending completions after restart follow the original routing\n- ACP `streamTo` stays separate; `announceTarget` is native-only and never maps to ACP streaming\n\n## Evidence\n\n- New/updated tests: spawn tool schema, spawn registration (incl. thread-bound cases), announce delivery routing (parent `deliver:false`, no channel fallback, idempotent retries), config schema precedence — all pass\n- Full local `check:changed` (CI lane, `CI=1`) passes at branch head: lint, prod/test types, boundary guards, import cycles\n- `config:docs:gen`/`check` clean; generated config reference updated\n",
